## Two honesty findings worth the whole round
1. **Flip-invariance bug class**: ratio momentum on negated levels (yields→"returns") is a no-op (`(−a)/(−b)=a/b`), silently building *anti*-momentum with inverted returns (SR −0.48 before fix). Any sleeve trading inverted series must flip the trend *sign*, not the levels.
2. **Same-day vol scaling lookahead** in per-asset inverse-vol weights — fixed with `.shift(1)`; flagged for audit of existing library CTA sleeves. Also: `data.ff_mom()` is broken (parse error) — workaround documented.

